{
  "id": "a64-image-theorem",
  "goals": [
    "∃ b', BootReach h (protectedBytes B n) (fetchFrom b.core.mem B (codeWords n)) b b' ∧ fetchFrom b.core.mem B (codeWords n) b'.core.pc = some (encode .hvc0) ∧ b'.core.x 0 = 0x84000008 ∧ b'.uartDone = true ∧ b'.core.out = b.core.out ++ LeanExe.Native.encodeWord (f x) ++ [0]",
    "LeanExe.A64.ProgramRuns m k args room cap .word (LeanExe.Native.encodeWord (f x)) fun _ => False",
    "LeanExe.A64.ProgramRuns m k args room cap .array (LeanExe.Native.encodeArray (f x)) fun c => c = 4",
    "LeanExe.A64.stackBound m k ≤ room.toNat",
    "(Verified.initialHeap compiled.tables).top.toNat + compiled.f.bound x ≤ 65536 * LeanExe.A64.initialPages compiled.module",
    "LeanExe.A64.entryOk m k [.f64] 1 .word = true",
    "w.toInt64.toInt = spec a b in an Image theorem",
    "an A64 Image theorem whose output names Real.exp, Real.sin, or a specification over ℤ",
    "LeanExe.A64.InputRuns m k n room cap o Out T for a program that reads its arguments from the UART",
    "P.rx.Delivers (ws.flatMap bytesOf) or P.rx.Flagged j for the PL011's receiver",
    "a bare-metal A64 program that polls a device's status register before each read",
    "LeanExe.A64.BytesRuns m k inMax room cap Out T for a program that reads a message of bytes from the UART",
    "P.normal P.uart = false or P.normal (P.uart + 0x18) = false for the platform of a boot state",
    "a run with a break on the UART's line, or whose input ends before the program's last read",
    "a theorem of a static Linux executable for AArch64 from its entry to exit_group",
    "LeanExe.A64.ElfLoaded (byteAt n) p.core.mem",
    "LeanExe.A64.elfSegments (byteAt n) = LeanExe.A64.elfSegmentsOf (LeanExe.A64.elfLayout m k inMax room cap)",
    "LeanExe.A64.SysBytesRuns m k inMax room cap Out T",
    "LeanExe.A64.StampRunsAny m k inMax room cap pin pout Out Tr",
    "an address that a routine computes from X17 after a call of a compiled function",
    "an allocation of inMax + 33 bytes against the bound of alloc_spec_runs",
    "the run of a WASI command's static Linux executable for AArch64 from its entry to exit_group",
    "the initial SP that Linux gives a process, after a runtime that sets SP before main",
    "an address in the data segment of genElfWith, whose layout depends on the program's length",
    "the startup routine's outcome of a WASI executable that checks descriptor 3, status 67 or the granted launch",
    "a WASI executable's theorem without a guest trap for a class of reply sequences"
  ],
